I am wondering if we should take this PR now and after #35037 is approved re-visit this and re-implement the functionality of Vector64/128.Create() with one operand in C# using AdvSimd.DuplicateToVector64/128(). 

Basically, this would mean that we leverage the JIT implementation of Vector64/128.Create() for DuplicateToVector64/128() (this would require only cosmetic changes in the JIT) and add the following to the C# files
```c#
if (AdvSimd.IsSupported)
{
  return AdvSimd.DuplicateToVector128(value);
}
```

This would be keep consistency with implementation on x86
@tannergooding @kunalspathak What do you think?
